-- title:
--   Candidate Bernstein matrices for heights 134.4–135
-- statement:
--   Store the rational power matrix $A$, an intermediate row-transform matrix $R$, and a proposed Bernstein matrix $B$, each with 12 rows and 23 columns, for a candidate polynomial on heights $t\in[134.4,135]$. Also define the finite Bernstein change-of-basis map. The stored matrices are data: their transform identities and lower bounds are separate certificates.
-- source:
--   Exact rational Bernstein framework adapted from sometik179; the candidate xi polynomial uses the theta/Mellin framework due to Gabewhigham.

/- Exact rational matrices for a candidate xi-polynomial Bernstein check.
The tables are data; their correctness and lower bounds are separate theorems. -/
